      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Hard to rule too many of these out. SUPERLIV (7) crossed from a wide gate to lead and was only denied in the final stages of a similar race to this at Geelong 18 days ago. Very fit after three runs back from a spell. Likely to race on the speed again and will prove tough to catch. BOLD BORDEAUX (1) began awkwardly then ran into traffic so his last start ninth over this trip at Geelong is better than it looks. Very fit and should give a good account with even luck. RESTLESS WIND (5) is back after a four-month spell. Yet to miss the frame in five runs, the highlight a third behind the smart Signature Scent at Caulfield in July. Has the class to test this field. SOUTHERN CRESCENT (3) has been in the money eight out of eight at this distance. Must be respected.",
